So each document has a list of tags and links to potential parents, as tags form a tree. All tags which are related to a particular document and relations between them are those directly accessible by fetching only one document. This is all good.

But the issue comes when I want to make faceted/filter search on top of those tags over multiple documents, all documents matching a query. I would like not just to have a set of filter based on values of tags, but also display them in a tree. So I think what I need is that I could aggregate all those `tags` fields of all documents into an union of all those lists, seen as sets. That would give me a long list of all tags existing in all documents matching the query and relations between them. The issue is, I could not find aggregation for this. I do understand that I could use [scripting](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/current/search-aggregations-metrics-scripted-metric-aggregation.html) to do this, but I think having it as a built-in aggregation could be faster, taking an advantage of set behavior of those lists and fact that one can deduplicate them much faster by using indices.

