**Description**
When we wrap our [EuiSwitch](https://github.com/elastic/eui/blob/master/src/components/form/switch/switch.tsx) in a `FormRow` component, we can pass an `aria-describedby` to add a secondary "helper" label. While reviewing an issue in Kibana, I think we would be better served to apply the FormRow label ID as a second aria-labelledby ID. This way the switch will have a combined `label ID + spanID` accessible label.

---
<img width="548" alt="Code snippet of EuiSwitch with a FormRow wrapper" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/934879/136417063-cfa7f19a-572c-4b2b-8f10-d181a2894de6.png">


**Meta-code solution**
```diff
! https://github.com/elastic/eui/blob/master/src/components/form/switch/switch.tsx#L108

const switchRowId = htmlIdGenerator('switch_row')();

<EuiFormRow
  label={<span id={switchRowId}>Label above switch</span>}>
  <button
      id={switchId}
      aria-checked={checked || false}
      className="euiSwitch__button"
      role="switch"
      type={type}
      disabled={disabled}
      onClick={onClick}
      aria-label={showLabel ? undefined : (label as string)}
-   aria-labelledby={showLabel ? labelId : undefined}
+   aria-labelledby={showLabel ? switchRowId showLabel ?? showLabel : undefined}
    {...rest}
  >
  ...
</EuiFormRow>
```

