Data Grid leaks memory when navigating between pages.

Minimum app to reproduce the problem: 
https://codesandbox.io/s/reverent-lamport-xwx8z (Works but complains about` Could not find module in path: '@elastic/eui/lib/components/icon/assets/expandMini.js' relative to '/node_modules/@elastic/eui/lib/components/icon/icon.js'`);

Steps to reproduce:
- Navigate through data using pagination
- Take snapshot of the memory heap in developer tools
- Observe the increase of Detached HTMLDivElement's and increase in memory consumption

Minimal code

```javascript
function useColumns() {
  const keys = [...Array(20).keys()].map((v) => `column_${v}`);
  const [visibleColumns, setVisibleColumns] = useState(keys);
  const columns = keys.map((id) => ({ id }));

  return { columns, columnVisibility: { visibleColumns, setVisibleColumns } };
}

function App() {
  const rowCount = 1200;
  const [pagination, setPagination] = useState({ pageIndex: 0, pageSize: 10 });
  const { columns, columnVisibility } = useColumns();

  const onChangePage = useCallback((pageIndex) => setPagination(({ pageSize }) => ({ pageIndex, pageSize })), []);
  const onChangeItemsPerPage = useCallback((pageSize) => setPagination(({ pageIndex }) => ({ pageIndex, pageSize })), []);

  const renderCellValue = useCallback(() => (Math.random()), []);

  return (
    <EuiDataGrid
      columns={columns}
      columnVisibility={columnVisibility}
      pagination={{
        ...pagination,
        pageSizeOptions: [10, 50, 100],
        onChangeItemsPerPage,
        onChangePage
      }}
      renderCellValue={renderCellValue}
      rowCount={rowCount}
      toolbarVisibility={false}
    />
  );
}
```

Possible cause of the leak can be found [in the following code section](https://github.com/elastic/eui/blob/master/src/components/datagrid/data_grid.tsx#L778).
 `Map` holds the reference to the DataGridCells [updateFocus](https://github.com/elastic/eui/blob/master/src/components/datagrid/data_grid_cell.tsx#L116) function which in turn holds the reference to the actual HTMLDivElement. When React calls the components willUnmount hook `Map` is cloned and from the cloned `Map` is removed the reference 
to the `updateFocus` function. As the HTMLDivElement is still not disposed and the orginal `Map` still holds the reference to the `updateFunction` it looks like it's not garbage collected even if it gets out of the scope.

Proposed solution would be not to clone the `Map` but to remove the given reference from it and return it.
```javascript
return () => {
  setCellsUpdateFocus(cellsUpdateFocus => {
    cellsUpdateFocus .delete(key);
    returncellsUpdateFocus;
 });
};
```

Heap [screenshots](https://imgur.com/a/S2Rez1B) before and after applying the proposed fix.

