## Problem

When using `EuiBasicTable` with an actions column, `DefaultItemAction.color` only applies to the **expanded** (inline) view. In the **collapsed** overflow menu (the `...` popover), the `color` property is ignored — every action renders with the default text color regardless of its `color` value.

This makes it impossible to render a danger-colored delete action in the overflow menu using the native API.

## Current workaround

We use a ReactNode `name` with `useLayoutEffect` and DOM traversal to find the parent `.euiBasicTable__collapsedAction` button and set `style.color` to the danger color:

```tsx
const DangerActionName = ({ children }) => {
  const ref = useRef(null);
  const { euiTheme } = useEuiTheme();
  useLayoutEffect(() => {
    const button = ref.current?.closest('.euiBasicTable__collapsedAction');
    if (button) {
      button.style.color = euiTheme.colors.textDanger;
      return () => { button.style.color = ''; };
    }
  }, [euiTheme.colors.textDanger]);
  return <EuiTextColor color="danger"><span ref={ref}>{children}</span></EuiTextColor>;
};
```

This is fragile — it depends on the internal class name `.euiBasicTable__collapsedAction` and direct DOM mutation.

## Proposal

Forward `action.color` to the `EuiContextMenuItem` rendered in `collapsed_item_actions` — similar to how it's already forwarded to `EuiButtonIcon` / `EuiButtonEmpty` in the expanded view.

## Questions

Is there a known alternative we're missing? Or would this be a welcome addition?

