When a Vega visualization query requests more than the 10,000 document default limit (governed by vis_type_vega.max_url_results), the data is silently truncated to 10,000 documents. The visualization renders with this partial data, but there is no error message, UI warning, or console log indicating that the dataset was limited.

This "silent failure" is misleading and can lead to incorrect data analysis, as the user assumes they are visualizing the full dataset requested by their query (e.g., 20,000 documents) when they are only seeing 10,000.

To Reproduce Steps to reproduce the behavior:

Ensure you have an index with more than 10,000 documents (e.g., 20,000 documents).

Go to OpenSearch Dashboards -> 'Visualize' library.

Click on 'Create Visualization' and select 'Vega'.

Use a Vega specification that explicitly requests more than 10,000 documents using the size parameter in the url body.

Sample Vega Spec:

JSON

{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "data": {
    "url": {
      "index": "index",
      "body": {
        "size": 20000 
      }
    },
    "format": {"property": "hits.hits"}
  },
  "mark": "point",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {"field": "_source.YOUR_FIELD_NAME_X", "type": "quantitative"},
    "y": {"field": "_source.YOUR_FIELD_NAME_Y", "type": "quantitative"}
  }
}
Run the visualization and observe the rendered chart.

Open the 'Inspect' panel and check the response. You will see that only 10,000 hits were processed, even though 20,000 were requested.

Notice that no error or warning message is displayed anywhere in the UI.

Expected behavior

The system should not fail silently. There are two expected behaviors:

(Ideal) A clear warning message should be displayed in the visualization panel, such as: "Query returned 20,000 hits but visualization is limited to the default 10,000. To view more, increase vis_type_vega.max_url_results in opensearch_dashboards.yml."

(Acceptable) The visualization should fail to render and show an explicit error message stating that the requested query size (20,000) exceeds the configured limit (10,000).

Silent truncation of data is unexpected and leads to confusion.

Dashboards Version 2.18.0

Plugins This occurs with the default plugins bundled with the 2.18.0 distribution.

Screenshots [If applicable, add a screenshot of the 'Inspect' panel showing only 10,000 hits, and the visualization that appears "normal" but is factually incomplete.]



Additional context

We are aware that the 10,000 document limit is a configurable default (vis_type_vega.max_url_results) intended for performance.

However, the bug is the lack of user feedback. This behavior forces users to discover this setting only after they coincidentally realize their data is incomplete, which is very difficult to debug. Improving the user experience by making this limit obvious (via a warning or error) when it is exceeded would be a significant improvement.

